 architectural community on there  that is able to help each other out  there's been a couple questions asked  from different people all over the world  and it's just incredible to see this  community growing and this community  coming together  it makes me looking at a camera and  talking to a camera feel a little bit  more real  otherwise it just feels like i'm a  little bit crazy talking to a camera in  a room all by myself  so i'd appreciate it if you check out  the links down below hit the subscribe  button if you want to continue seeing  these videos  and also hit the like button to help  with the youtube algorithm there's only  three apps i really use on this ipad  from an architectural point of view  that i can't fault morfolio trace is  number one  i'm not sponsored in any way shape  performed by them i've done a little bit  of work  just promoting them before because i  really genuinely like the app  but nothing from the company so morfolio  trace is incredible  adobe photoshop is becoming more and  more handy on the ipad just to simply  fix up bits and pieces that aren't  correct  and finally apple notes it is the  simplest app of all time  but it's just so easy to draw and markup  on and sketch up a detail to send to  somebody who needs to  or if you're in a meeting with a client  and they're asking you how does this  work  in real life you can sketch up that  detail in  seconds and it just makes that  experience of using the ipad  as an architect and using the skills  that you've developed over a lifetime  so much easier to convey than they ever  have before  now the simplest reason i recommend the  ipad pro  over every other ipad is the screen  i didn't buy the 12.9 even though the  screen is phenomenally better  but i think the screen on the 11 inch is  so good  that there's not much better that you  can get if you compare them side by side  yes you'll see the difference  yes you'll know that the 12.9 is a  better resolution display  but with the 11 inch you're never going  to know that  the screen is so good that it doesn't  matter anymore  it doesn't matter how good the screen  gets beyond this that 11 inch ipad pro  at 120 hertz with full refresh rate  and just how crystal clear it is  can't be beaten now what's my overall  verdict i guess if you're an architect  or if you're an architecture student  it's yes and no  if you're an architecture student i  wouldn't recommend the ipad pro  or any other ipad for the simple fact it  can't run any architectural software  so you're definitely going to need to  run autocad  archicad revit potentially rendering  softwares  like enscape twin motion you could go up  to unreal  engine you could go all the way through  to the high-end rendering packages  that an ipad can more than likely handle  but just isn't there from a software  point of view if this changes in the  near future with ipad os 15  and they introduce something that allows  you to run it like a laptop where you  can  actually run architectural software  throw that opinion out the window  go buy one today because as a product it  is phenomenal for all architecture  students  i think it is perfect for anybody at  university if it could do that  until then i'd still recommend a good  laptop over an ipad and then of course  a desktop over everything else because  as an architecture student  you just go through an abundance of  different programs trying to get  all that information down on paper  trying to get a good grade as an  architect on the other hand  i think it's a fine line architects  obviously have a variety of different  roles and an architect can be  a completely different role in itself  you could be an architect that literally  just sits at a computer and designs  all day long or you could be an  architect that liaises with clients  sits at the computer does administrative  roles runs their own business  has more of a senior management role if  you have that senior management role  where  you are required to do some  administrative things some client  liaising  and anything in between there yes hands  down  ipad pro with the new m1 chip is  miles better than anything we've ever  had before  and probably will be for a couple  seasons now until they come up with an  m5 or something like that  where it supersedes this incredibly for  everybody else that might be watching  this video it doesn't matter what  position you're in or what industry  you're in  if you're in some sort of leadership  role or if you're just a student  that doesn't require any architectural  programs that's just going to run word  excel things like that i think the ipad  has just  surpassed the laptop anyway that's all  for me today guys thank you so much for  watching i hope you enjoyed the video  if you did make sure you smash that  subscribe button down below make sure  you also hit that like button to help  with the youtube algorithm  and as always i'll see you next monday
 

